{"question_id": "alg-lim-02", "sib_category": "mathematics", "corpus_category": "mathematics", "difficulty": "hard", "evaluation_method": "SYMBOLIC", "target": "splex", "outcome": "CORRECT", "credit": 1.0, "detail": "literal match for E", "latency_ms": 12921, "ttft_ms": 1298, "routed_display_name": "Nemotron 3 Super", "routed_category": "Mathematics", "cortex_version": "v1", "routed_model_id": null, "prompt_tokens": null, "completion_tokens": null, "cost_usd": null, "conversation_id": "7cea0427-43ed-4a45-a57a-f84e44d852f0", "message_id": "7a6b777d-7f4e-4f46-9ad4-639c4dd710a8", "response_excerpt": "We evaluate  \n\n\\[\nL=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\Bigl(1+\\frac1x\\Bigr)^{x}.\n\\]\n\nTake the natural logarithm:\n\n\\[\n\\ln L=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty} x\\ln\\!\\Bigl(1+\\frac1x\\Bigr).\n\\]\n\nFor small \\(t\\), \\(\\ln(1+t)=t-\\frac{t^{2}}{2}+O(t^{3})\\).  \nHere \\(t=\\frac1x\\to0\\), so\n\n\\[\n\\ln\\!\\Bigl(1+\\frac1x\\Bigr)=\\frac1x-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}}+O\\!\\Bigl(\\frac1{x^{3}}\\Bigr).\n\\]\n\nMultiply by \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\nx\\ln\\!\\Bigl(1+\\frac1x\\Bigr)=1-\\frac{1}{2x}+O\\!\\Bigl(\\frac1{x^{2}}\\Bigr)\\xrightarrow[x\\to\\infty]{}1.\n\\]\n\nThus  \n\n\\[\n\\ln L = 1 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad L = e^{1}=e.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{e}\n\\]", "review_criteria": []}
